            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Criticisms and Public Image</strong><br>\nDespite his philanthropy, Rockefeller faced criticism for the ruthless methods his company used to control the oil market. His public image varied from a shrewd businessman to a generous benefactor.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Family and Legacy</strong><br>\nHis family continued his legacy of wealth and philanthropy, establishing numerous institutions, including the University of Chicago and the Rockefeller University. His descendants remain influential in business and philanthropy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Enduring Influence</strong><br>\nRockefeller passed away in 1937 at the age of 97. His influence extended beyond his lifetime, shaping the fields of business and philanthropy, and setting a precedent for corporate structure and charitable work.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
